+# Shared Alerts actual one-owner cohort
+
+This additive source/native checkpoint follows [the complete Shared inventory](shared-functional-acceptance-20261119.md). It preserves the frozen12-case source and prior packet unchanged. [Fixed evidence](shared-same-owner-cohort-evidence-20261119.json) records this checkpoint's exact source/result hashes and [two-file source-only patch](shared-same-owner-cohort-source-20261119.patch). Coordinator owns integration/current runtime admission. No production action.
+
+## Actual provider discovery
+
+Coordinator's read-only actual discovery at `2026-11-19T03:39:22Z` found ONE true Discord owner across both authorized guilds. The owner is an approved selector and active Platform user; private identity values stay in the existing supporting evidence and are not copied here. Evidence `/home/traderlink/projects/traderslink-coordinator/operations/community-two-guild-owner-cohort-readonly-20261119.json`, SHA256 `2fcceedd196d934540f4e11724241cb6576dff4fbd3a1a071abe78a5709ea056`:two provider GETs,zero provider/database writes,no token/session export. Existing stage evidence had Tests owner membership and no stored Main membership. This is ownership discovery only, not current source/case admission.
+
+Do not create two fake native owners,mark the other selector guild_owner,borrow the executor's admin SELF proof,transfer server ownership or add an out-of-scope guild. The prior12-case separate-owner fixtures remain valid local business-method coverage but do not describe the actually available owner cohort. Genuine separate publisher membership/grants must be verified and normally configured when that variant is used.
+
+## Current business contract and new native evidence
+
+`shared-alerts-same-owner-native.test.ts` uses real migrated disposable SQLite and real Core/Shared repository methods,one local seeded owner across two different guild-backed communities,and a separate non-owner publisher. Private hosted identity values are not copied. Four tests PASS:
+
+1. TestsGeneral to designated main alerts: independent receiver acceptance,same owner in two different community contexts,source-context approval denied,nonowner publisher review denied,receiving owner review accepted. Covers both separate-publisher and owner-authored content.
+2. Reverse direction with the same independent contexts and checks.
+3. Two simultaneous opposite-direction agreements: accepting one does not accept the other despite a common owner.
+4. Same-community sharing denied; removing native Main owner evidence does not remove Tests ownership or let Tests proof authorize Main.
+
+The current rule is RECEIVING COMMUNITY owner approval. It has no independent author-user!=reviewer-user prohibition: the true common owner may approve their own authored alert from the receiving community context. A source context cannot do so,even for the same user. A non-owner publisher cannot review as the receiving owner. This is an observed existing contract,not a newly implemented relaxation. No current business incompatibility with legitimate same-owner cross-guild sharing was found.
+
+These fixtures do not prove actual hosted owner/publisher access,normal source UI/common queue creation,controller admission,original browser POST rejection or Discord delivery. No product source changes or provider requests were made.
+
+## Genuine missing-membership preparation
+
+The current Community-owned `verifyCommunityRequestMember` supports normal authenticated guild/member observation and `PlatformDiscordMembershipRepository.upsertCurrent`. `guildOwner` comes from the actual guild owner response compared with the actual active identity; do not insert a guessed owner bit. Main needs the capability-bound exact staging guild override,current real session/Auth/erasure observation commit frame,normal target/freshness checks and bounded provider GETs. Keep I/O outside transactions and commit observation only after unchanged target/dependency/live-principal checks.
+
+This method requires an existing native community and identity. It updates an EXISTING Community membership; it does not create the community or insert a missing Community membership. Qualify those facts first and use the normal admitted Community onboarding/join path where absent. Bot-owner metadata alone is not a complete native fixture. Refresh of stored provider evidence does not mint a new session or grant arbitrary publish/review permission.
+
+The finite delivery capability must admit actual source and receiver native ownership separately,even when the owner user is equal. Exact community/guild/destination/route/consent/payload/revision bindings remain different. Generic workers remain disabled; current-image browser/provider QA stays open.
+
+## Verification
+
+Focused new suite:4/4PASS,7.89s total,367ms native assertions. Private JSON `/tmp/shared-same-owner-native-20261119-rcee35a2/result.json`. Targeted ESLint and diff-check PASS. One worker,no file parallelism,private config/cache/output; common flock and owned feature lock released. MemAvailable4,503,684KiB before/4,259,244KiB after,observed memory pressure zero,cgroup max unbounded. Prior unchanged12-case suite was not redundantly rerun. Help review: test/documentation only,no product guide update needed; current browser Help verification remains open.
